      "key": {
        "uuid": "147df8d0_5ae25199",
        "filename": "core/java/android/app/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T20:20:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A nice to have thing: There is a similar API in R, https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ApplicationExitInfo?hl\u003den#getTraceInputStream(), it only returns the ANR traces now. Maybe we could hook them up later to return the tombstone traces as well.",
      "revId": "1682c4a26b99bd6c0667fa3647836b7290bb2974",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52dc9eaf_10f10720",
        "filename": "core/java/android/app/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T22:22:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That was my original plan, but I\u0027m not sure we can provide all of the fields that ApplicationExitInfo provides (getImportance and getProcessStateSummary primarily, and getPss/getRss as well, although it looks like the javadoc for those allows us to return 0 for those.)\n\nThe semantics of packageName in getHistoricalProcessExitReasons would be different as well: I don\u0027t think we can differentiate between packages in the same UID (we don\u0027t know the package name!).\n\nGiven that, do you think we should implement this in ApplicationExitInfo?",
      "parentUuid": "147df8d0_5ae25199",
      "revId": "1682c4a26b99bd6c0667fa3647836b7290bb2974",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1012b771_93065873",
        "filename": "core/java/android/app/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T22:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe not to change the getHistoricalProcessExitReasons(). \n\nAs there are fields \u0027pid/uid\u0027 in the tombstone proto, we may associate it with each ApplicationExitInfo record. \n\nSo the procedure would be like this: an app process crashed and restarted. The system_server gets notified and checks if there is a tombstone file for that crash, via the NativeTombstoneManager API, searches the returned tombstone files and compares the pid/uid, and then creates the ApplicationExitInfo record internally. The subsequent app process will be able to call getHistoricalProcessExitReasons() to get the most recent crash record, and then call ApplicationExitInfo.getTraceInputStream(), which will return the FileDescriptor that NativeTombstoneManager holds.",
      "parentUuid": "52dc9eaf_10f10720",
      "revId": "1682c4a26b99bd6c0667fa3647836b7290bb2974",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25e2ed5b_dc5a4252",
        "filename": "core/java/android/app/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T22:44:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, but if they provide a package name to getHistoricalProcessExitReasons, we might give them native tombstones generated from other apps with the same UID. Maybe that\u0027s okay? I\u0027ll move over to integrating with getHistoricalProcessExitReasons.",
      "parentUuid": "1012b771_93065873",
      "revId": "1682c4a26b99bd6c0667fa3647836b7290bb2974",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
